ne of  those things that's that's ridiculous  khan only ended up appearing on the  radio show after his assistant who is  from cleveland called into bull and fox  to discuss the brown's most recent win  the actor eventually joined the  conversation delighting fans by sharing  that an elf sequel very nearly happened  and that he had been ready to sign on  this was of course a major shift from  his reluctance to appear in the first  film khan told the radio show hosts that  he had initially turned down the request  to play farrell's father all right uh  let's get it over with  as khan said will called me one night  and said jimmy want to do this picture  with me  can't reply to farrell's request  negatively at first saying listen will i  love you you're a funny guy but i'm not  doing a picture called elf okay khan  said he negotiated to change the film  title to elk on the working scripts as a  condition of his casting adding i said  i'll tell you what if you put a k on the  end of it like just through the working  scripts then i'll do it it was great fun  with will he's a great guy following the  incredible success of elf the actor  shared that he was ready for a sequel  despite the film's two biggest creatives  butting heads khan revealed we were  gonna do it and i thought oh my god i  finally got a franchise movie i could  make some money let my kids do what the  hell they want to do however personality  clashes may not be the only reason we  haven't seen an elf two yet both favreau  and farrow keep pretty busy the director  is currently attached to several disney  projects including season three of the  mandalorian meanwhile the saturday night  live alum continues his on-screen work  in surprise hits like eurovision song  contest the story of fire saga as he  juggles producing obligations on  projects like succession and dead to me  sadly it seems like the odds of an elf 2  occurring just got even lower as james  khan tragically passed away on july 6  2022. khan's